system "BSI:kor-Kore:Latn:6505-1982-t8" {

metadata {
  authority_id bsi
  id 6505-1982-t8
  language iso-639-2:kor
  source_script Kore
  destination_script Latn
  name "PD 6505:1982 Table VIII - The Romanization of All Letters in Sino-Korean Words"
  url ""
  creation_date 1982
  adoption_date
  description {    PD 6505:1982, Guide to the romanization of Korean, Table VIII
    (source p26): the Sino-Korean-specific layer of the guide. Values
    are McCune-Reischauer-style: o-breve for the ㅓ series, u-macron
    for ㅡ, w-compounds, the intervocalic voiced forms -g- -d- -b-
    -j- -r-, the syllable-final assimilation grid (-ngn- -ngm- -kt-
    -ls- -rh-), silent initial ㅇ, ㅆ romanized ss-, and a hyphen
    between syllables (the document's own convention in its
    bracketed examples). Transcribed visually from the scan at 8-10x.
    The guide's mechanical system (Part Four) is a separate map.
  }

  notes {
    note "VOWELS (read at 10x): a ae ya yae ŏ e yŏ ye o wa wae oe yo
    u wŏ we wi yu ū ūi i. The o-series breve and the u-macron are the
    document's own printed diacritics (the u-mark is a straight bar
    in the scan, distinct from the o-breve cups)."
    note "INITIALS: k- n- t- (r-) m- p- s- [ㅇ not romanized initially,
    per the source's note under the table] ch- ch'- k'- t'- p'- h-,
    and ss- (the source states ㅆ also occurs as the initial letter of
    Sino-Korean words). Intervocalic voicing per the grid's Vowel
    row: -g- -d- -b- -j- -r-."
    note "ASSIMILATION GRID (syllable-final x next-syllable-initial,
    cells read at 8x; encoded as pair rules spanning the syllable
    hyphen): ㄱ row -kk- -ngn- -kt- -ngn- -ngm- -kp- -ks- / ㄴ row -ng-
    -nn- -nd- -ll- -nm- -nb- -ns- / ㄹ row -lg- -ll- -lt- -ll- -lm-
    -lb- -ls- -r- / ㅁ row -mg- -mn- -md- -mn- -mm- -mb- -ms- / ㅂ row
    -pk- -mn- -pt- -mn- -mm- -pp- -ps- -b- / ㅇ row -ngg- -ngn- -ngd-
    -ngn- -ngm- -ngb- -ngs- -ng- (plus the ch ch' k' t' p' h columns:
    -kch- -kch'- -kk'- -kt'- -kp'- -kh- / -nj- -nch'- -nk'- -nt'-
    -np'- -nh- / -lch- -lch'- -lk'- -lt'- -lp'- -rh- / -mj- -mch'-
    -mk'- -mt'- -mp'- -mh- / -pch- -pch'- -pk'- -pt'- -pp'- -ph- /
    -ngj- -ngch'- -ngk'- -ngt'- -ngp'- -ngh-). The ㄹ row's ㅇ column
    is -r- (ㄹ renders r before a vowel-initial syllable). Finals
    before ㅇ-initial syllables otherwise render plain across the
    hyphen, matching the source's own [ki-ŏk] and [kun-ŏ] examples."
    note "SOURCE RULES under the table, quoted: ㅇ is not romanized
    when it is the initial letter of a syllable. If the vowel is i-
    or y-, it may be taken as ni- or ny- after consonants in special
    cases, see ¶.22 (special-case epenthesis: recorded, not
    mechanically encoded). Initial ㄹ r- occurs only in foreign words
    in South Korean, but also in Korean words in the North Korean
    spelling. For -lt- as -ld- and -lch- as -ll- in special cases,
    see ¶.10 (recorded, not encoded; the grid's default cells are
    what this map applies)."
    note "COVERAGE: Table VIII covers the 14 basic consonants + ㅆ and
    the 21 simple and compound vowels. Syllables with tense initials
    (ㄲ ㄸ ㅃ ㅉ), cluster finals, or letters outside the table pass
    through unchanged: the source states that letters not in Table
    VIII and all vernacular words are covered in its Parts ii and
    iii. Generated by tools/gen-pd6505-t8.py."
  }
}

tests {
   "군어" ->  "kun-ŏ"
   "기억" ->  "ki-ŏk"
   "한자" ->  "han-ja"
   "국민" ->  "kung-min"
   "국어" ->  "kuk-ŏ"
   "부산" ->  "pu-san"
   "조선" ->  "cho-sŏn"
   "감사" ->  "kam-sa"
   "학교" ->  "hak-kyo"
   "가인" ->  "ka-in"
   "일년" ->  "il-lyŏn"
   "의주" ->  "ūi-ju"
   "국물" ->  "kung-mul"
   "참외" ->  "ch'am-oe"
}

